course: dictionary
lesson: 15937
title: Unrivalled
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unrivalled means better than all the others, with nothing equal to it. When you meet it, ask yourself: is this the very best, with nothing close to it? «The museum has an unrivalled collection of dinosaur bones.» No other collection is as good, so this one is the best of all.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. Adverts and travel books often use it to praise things: «The hotel offers an unrivalled view of the sea.» If a view is unrivalled, no other view could match it. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The hotel offers a view with nothing equal to it» still makes sense.
explain: Sports reports use it too: «She showed unrivalled speed in the race.» Speed that nobody could match is unrivalled speed. It is a strong word, so save it for things that are truly the best.
fact: Unrivalled means better than all the others, with nothing equal to it.
fact: «Unrivalled» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «unrivalled skill».
fact: Common phrases include «unrivalled view», «unrivalled knowledge» and «unrivalled success».
fact: In British English it is spelled unrivalled; in American English it is spelled unrivaled.
fact: A rival is someone who competes with you, so unrivalled means nobody is competing at that level.
exercise: «The chef's cakes are unrivalled in the whole town.» What does unrivalled mean here? | Burnt and cold | Very small | *Better than all the others | Shared with everyone
exercise: «Her knowledge of the stars is unrivalled.» Which word is closest in meaning? | Ordinary | Broken | Hidden | *Unmatched
exercise: «The team had unrivalled success that year.» What does this tell you about the team? | Lost every game | They were new to the game | *They were the best, with no equal | They played only one match
test: Which word in «The view from the top was unrivalled» means better than all the others? | was | view | *unrivalled | top
test: Which phrase uses unrivalled correctly? | a slow, unrivalled walk to school | *an unrivalled view of the mountains | an unrivalled, wet sock
exam: Which of these best matches the meaning of unrivalled? | *Second to none | Cheap | Ordinary | Old
